sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Brassica oleracea Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 172 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 overall 88.81. Closes the Pass 1 gaps without raising the nonlinear sweep correlation. Modal sigma(k) Pearson r is 0.9999999522 (RMSE 0.0036, KS 0.167) against reference gate 0.98. The D_v sweep stays at r = 0.8266 with its own RMSE, and analytical wavelength increases on 5/5 steps. Equal-diffusion ablation std is 0.00051 against pattern std 1.586, and sigma_max changes from +0.551 to -0.100. Curd circularity is 0.583 against a circle null of 1. GIF cv_sim_similarity is 88.4 at 640x480 and 12 frames. Cell-scale sigma at 15 µm is -14.56; the 100 µm tier is +0.406, below the 172 µm peak. Overall 88.8/100 (faithfulness 87.9, reproducibility 90.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 697207 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 febada1318b9e5a6db50dda52257067810cf7e7ff0ffdd998737e9b9de014e9c (sha256 febada1318b9e5a6db50dda52257067810cf7e7ff0ffdd998737e9b9de014e9c), spec_fingerprint eace5cd4a6194a1b662909a5f49a87e8ba4e22bd4a0f6438065b99d8328eb65a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eace5cd4a6194a1b662909a5f49a87e8ba4e22bd4a0f6438065b99d8328eb65a; artifact_sha256: febada1318b9e5a6db50dda52257067810cf7e7ff0ffdd998737e9b9de014e9c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=40b5ed77e35bfbbd..., datasets/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=1cbb4e4e7defa706..., datasets/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=7306e7e95f1cbecc..., datasets/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=2bbca9157437d615..., datasets/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=6b0322cfb4700c55...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: linear dispersion selects a wavenumber k_c | Schnakenberg 1979: du/dt = a - u + u^2 v + Du lap u and dv/dt = b - u^2 v + Dv lap v | Azpeitia et al. 2021 DOI 10.1126/science.abg5999: Romanesco cones from a reiterated floral network | Duclos and Björkman 2008: the curd is proliferating inflorescence meristem; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian at a=0.10, b=0.90 and sigma(k) on a periodic grid | D_v = 51.752 so the fastest mode is 172 µm (13 px, 24 waves, 4128 µm patch) | Modal growth fit, D_v sweep with separate RMSE, equal-diffusion ablation, excess-green curd metrics; transfer_boundary: 172 µm is the MorphoEval detail length for slot 3137, not a figure in Azpeitia or Duclos | The animated field is a primordium-scale spot texture. The photograph is a macro curd. Fitness is statistical, not a registered overlay | 15 µm is the successor cell-scale boundary used to test stability, not a new measured epidermal diameter; does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg u and v are identified Brassica morphogens | That this wavelength model replaces the Azpeitia plastochron account | That the nonlinear sweep Pearson r exceeds 0.98 (it is 0.8266)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.888"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (MorphoEval loop 3137 Pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

